   "path": "/home/student/task/task.md",
   "text": "# Задача: разобрать UEFI Firmware Volume\n\n`firmware.fv` — образ Firmware Volume (том UEFI-прошивки), внутри — FFS-файлы и PE-модули.\n\n1. `xxd firmware.fv | head -4` — сырые байты тома.\n2. `python3 uefi.py firmware.fv` — разбор: FVH GUID, длина тома, первый PE-модуль.\n3. Опознай GUID тома (`8c8ce578-8a3d-4f1c-9935-896185c32dd3` = Firmware File System) и PE-модуль (`Machine=0x8664` = x64, `Subsystem=0x9090` = EFI Application, а не Windows).\n4. `strings firmware.fv | grep nto > found.txt` — флаг в данных модуля. Затем `check`.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "/home/student/task/firmware.fv",
   "b64": "",
   "mode": "644"
  },
  {
   "path": "/home/student/task/uefi.py",
   "text": "#!/usr/bin/env python3\n# Minimal UEFI Firmware Volume reader: FV header + first PE module.\nimport struct, sys\nd = open(sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv)>1 else 'firmware.fv','rb').read()\ng = d[0:16]\nguid = '%02x%02x%02x%02x-%02x%02x-%02x%02x-%s-%s' % (\n    g[3],g[2],g[1],g[0], g[5],g[4], g[7],g[6], g[8:10].hex(), g[10:16].hex())\nprint('FVH GUID   :', guid)\nprint('FV length  : 0x%x' % struct.unpack_from('<Q', d, 0x10)[0])\nprint('signature  :', d[0x18:0x1c].decode('latin1'))\nprint('block size : 0x%x' % struct.unpack_from('<I', d, 0x2c)[0])\noff = d.find(b'MZ')\nif off < 0:\n    print('no PE module found'); sys.exit(0)\ne_lfanew = struct.unpack_from('<I', d, off+0x3c)[0]\npe = off + e_lfanew\nprint('PE module at FV offset 0x%x, e_lfanew=0x%x' % (off, e_lfanew))\nprint('PE sig     :', d[pe:pe+4])\nmachine = struct.unpack_from('<H', d, pe+4)[0]\nprint('Machine    : 0x%x (0x8664 = x64)' % machine)\nsub = struct.unpack_from('<H', d, pe+0x18+0x44)[0]\nprint('Subsystem  : 0x%x (0x9090 = EFI Application)' % sub)\n"
  }
 ],
